{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>According to all that HaShem commanded.</b> The verse returns to say this thing a second time, and also immediately following a third time. Perhaps it is because they sinned in the [Golden] Calf in thought, in speech, and in deed — as I explained there — and in the aspect of each one they denied the entire Torah, and therefore in the rectification all three were together: the voluntary contribution is the deed; the thought is the aspect of wisdom in the craft; the speech is that they would say at the time of the deed 'for the sake of the commandment of HaShem,' as I explained earlier. Corresponding to all three the verse says that they did <b>as HaShem commanded Moses</b>, for they repaired the three evil gradations."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:37:18.509007707Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}